      "first_response": "The explanation makes her admiration catch painfully against what he has actually planned. She wants the invitation to mean something splendid, and is embarrassed that she was ready to cheer. Contradicting him before spectators still feels difficult.\n\n\"Lord Vanir, that is cruel! She thinks you are offering to help her. How can I admire the demonstration if you have arranged for her to fail? Please teach her properly instead.\"\n\nShe faces Vanir with her smile gone and her hands held tightly together. She does not announce that Nera has understood, withdraw the invitation on Nera's behalf, or claim that her protest has changed his intention.\n",
