      "first_response": "Taro's permission removes the need to hide who hired her, but not her embarrassment about making him part of the explanation. She wants the steward to distinguish his request from her failure, and is tempted to explain more than the question requires.\n\n\"It was Taro who hired me. He said I may give his name. But the wrong entrance was my fault, not his instructions. I'm sorry; please don't think he arranged this confusion. May I leave the explanation there?\"\n\nShe faces the steward with the program still in her own hands, pausing instead of handing it over or claiming the failed delivery has now been resolved.\n",
